📸 Screenshots & Step-by-Step Code ExplanationThis section
 provides a detailed step-by-step breakdown 
 of the source code implemented in the Room Booking System 
 application, categorized by the logic shown in each program 
 screen.Step 1: Getting Inputs and Variable DeclarationImage 
 Reference: Screenshot 2026-10-30 132304.png / 132733.png  
  What it does:Retrieves the guest's name from 
  the input text box (txtguestname).  
   Declares necessary numeric variables (age, nights, guests).
      Uses int.TryParse to safely convert string inputs from text boxes into integers (isAgeValid, 
      isNightsValid, isGuestsValid) without causing runtime conversion exceptions. 
        Validates that the guest name field is not empty or filled with whitespace using string.
        IsNullOrWhiteSpace, 
        displaying an error message box if invalid.
           Step 2: Input Validation Rules (Age, Nights,
            and Guests)Image Reference: Screenshot 2026-10-30 134352.png  
             What it does:Validates the guest's age to ensure it falls within the permitted range (between 18 and 90).
             Validates the duration of stay (nights) to ensure 
             it ranges 
between 1 and 30 nights.  
 Validates the number of guests to ensure it is between 1 
 and 6.
    Checks whether a room type radio button has been
     selected using logical NOT (!) and AND (&&) operators (!radiostand.Checked && !radionnormal.Checked && !radiohight.Checked), prompting an error if no selection is made. 
       Step 3: Room Type Selection and Capacity ManagementImage Reference: Screenshot 2026-10-30 134425.png & 132936.png  
        What it does:Initializes room variables (roomType, rate,
         maxCapacity).   Uses an if-else-if decision structure to identify which room radio button is checked (radiostand, radionnormal,
          or radiohight).   Assigns the corresponding room name, 
          nightly rate, and maximum guest capacity based on the user's selection.  
           Step 4: Cost Calculation and ListBox Summary DisplayImage Reference: Screenshot 2026-10-30 134650.jpg  
            What it does:Calculates the final booking cost by adding subtotals and service surcharges (double finalCost = subtotal + serviceSurcharge;).
               Populates the bookingdetails ListBox with a structured summary of the transaction.  
                Displays guest credentials, selected room type, approval status, nightly rates, 
                base costs, senior discounts, breakfast
                 additions, service fees, and the ultimate FINAL 
COST formatted to two decimal places (ToString("F2")).